1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,234
Photos, documents and downloads need a home on every site.

2
00:00:05,234 --> 00:00:10,196
The Media Library keeps them in folders, and any page can reuse them.

3
00:00:10,196 --> 00:00:15,555
In this video, you upload files, organize them in folders, rename, move and

4
00:00:15,555 --> 00:00:18,400
find them, and reuse them in content.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,882
A site uses many files:

6
00:00:24,882 --> 00:00:27,024
photos, PDFs and downloads.

7
00:00:27,024 --> 00:00:32,410
When they are scattered across pages, it is hard to know what the site holds.

8
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,929
The Media module gives the site one library.

9
00:00:35,929 --> 00:00:39,750
You manage its files and folders in the admin, and each file is

10
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:42,020
served from its own public address.

11
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:47,068
A media field on a page keeps the path of a file in the library.

12
00:00:47,068 --> 00:00:51,120
The file is stored once, and any number of pages can use it.

13
00:00:55,362 --> 00:00:59,013
In the admin menu, Media, Library opens the media library.

14
00:00:59,013 --> 00:01:03,578
The entry appears for users whose role has the Manage Media permission, or

15
00:01:03,578 --> 00:01:05,632
a permission that includes it.

16
00:01:06,085 --> 00:01:08,317
On the left is the folder tree.

17
00:01:08,317 --> 00:01:12,540
Its first entry, Files, is the root folder, and the files of the

18
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,135
selected folder are listed beside it.

19
00:01:15,649 --> 00:01:20,929
The list shows each file's Name, when it was Last modified, and its Size.

20
00:01:20,929 --> 00:01:23,469
Folders appear only in the tree.

21
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,619
Above the list, Upload files adds files from your computer.

22
00:01:27,619 --> 00:01:32,910
The trash can button deletes the selected files, and the download button downloads them.

23
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:40,120
Select the folder that should receive the files.

24
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:44,178
Click Upload files and choose one or more files, or drag files from

25
00:01:44,178 --> 00:01:46,068
your computer onto the page.

26
00:01:46,528 --> 00:01:50,524
The Uploads panel in the corner lists each file with its progress, and

27
00:01:50,524 --> 00:01:52,364
a check mark when it is done.

28
00:01:52,364 --> 00:01:54,468
The files then appear in the list.

29
00:01:54,932 --> 00:01:59,315
A file whose name already exists in the folder is refused with a warning:

30
00:01:59,315 --> 00:02:02,922
A file with this name already exists in the current folder.

31
00:02:07,222 --> 00:02:11,805
Point at a folder in the tree, and a button with three dots appears.

32
00:02:11,805 --> 00:02:16,822
Click it on Files to open the folder menu, which offers Create a subfolder.

33
00:02:17,349 --> 00:02:19,194
Choose Create a subfolder.

34
00:02:19,194 --> 00:02:21,906
The Create folder dialog asks for a name:

35
00:02:21,906 --> 00:02:24,329
type Harvest Festival, and click Ok.

36
00:02:29,101 --> 00:02:32,347
The folder is added to the tree under Files.

37
00:02:32,347 --> 00:02:37,930
Select it, and the breadcrumb above the list reads Files, then Harvest Festival,

38
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:40,981
while the page says This folder is empty.

39
00:02:41,475 --> 00:02:44,409
Every folder except Files also offers Delete.

40
00:02:44,409 --> 00:02:48,608
Choose it on Old Drafts, and the Delete folder dialog asks, Are you

41
00:02:48,608 --> 00:02:51,025
sure you want to delete this folder?

42
00:02:51,490 --> 00:02:56,760
With the default file storage, deleting a folder also deletes the files inside it.

43
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,658
Click Ok.

44
00:02:57,658 --> 00:03:01,670
Old Drafts leaves the tree, and the library returns to Files.

45
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:10,030
Each file has a menu with three dots at the end of its row.

46
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:13,989
It offers Rename, Move, Copy, View, Download and Delete.

47
00:03:14,449 --> 00:03:19,566
Rename opens the Rename file dialog, with the current name in the File name box.

48
00:03:19,566 --> 00:03:24,029
Type another name that keeps an allowed file extension, and click Ok.

49
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,718
Move opens the Move file dialog.

50
00:03:26,718 --> 00:03:31,136
In the Select a folder box, choose Harvest Festival and click Ok; the

51
00:03:31,136 --> 00:03:34,730
file leaves this list, and a message confirms the move.

52
00:03:35,193 --> 00:03:39,569
Copy works the same way, except that the original stays where it is.

53
00:03:39,569 --> 00:03:42,408
Click Ok, and a message confirms the copy.

54
00:03:42,408 --> 00:03:46,903
Open Harvest Festival, and the copy is there under the same name, next

55
00:03:46,903 --> 00:03:48,323
to the moved file.

56
00:03:48,802 --> 00:03:51,820
To work on several files, tick their check boxes.

57
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:55,937
The trash can and download buttons above the list show how many files

58
00:03:55,937 --> 00:03:58,572
are selected, and they act on all of them.

59
00:03:59,025 --> 00:04:03,499
Click the trash can button, and the Delete file dialog asks you to confirm.

60
00:04:03,499 --> 00:04:07,255
Click Ok, and the selected files are deleted from the library.

61
00:04:11,555 --> 00:04:13,513
Select Orchard Photos.

62
00:04:13,513 --> 00:04:19,599
By default the list shows ten files per page, so its twelve files take two pages.

63
00:04:19,599 --> 00:04:25,405
The pager below the list offers First, Previous, page numbers, Next and Last.

64
00:04:25,909 --> 00:04:29,553
Type in the Search and filter box to show only the files whose

65
00:04:29,553 --> 00:04:31,160
names contain your text.

66
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,519
The filter applies to the open folder.

67
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:38,033
Click the Name, Last modified or Size heading to sort by it, and

68
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:40,425
click it again to reverse the order.

69
00:04:40,884 --> 00:04:45,349
The grid button above the list switches to thumbnails for images; other files

70
00:04:45,349 --> 00:04:47,501
show an icon with their extension.

71
00:04:47,501 --> 00:04:49,814
Click it again to return to the list.

72
00:04:50,286 --> 00:04:53,102
The gear button opens the settings.

73
00:04:53,102 --> 00:04:58,048
Items per page offers 10, 20, 50 and 100 files, and Thumbnail size

74
00:04:58,048 --> 00:05:00,796
switches between Normal and Large.

75
00:05:01,304 --> 00:05:04,617
The drive button next to the gear shows Available Storage.

76
00:05:04,617 --> 00:05:08,343
With the default file storage, that is the free space on the drive

77
00:05:08,343 --> 00:05:09,844
that holds the library.

78
00:05:14,144 --> 00:05:17,778
A media field can open the library, so you pick a file instead

79
00:05:17,778 --> 00:05:19,274
of uploading it again.

80
00:05:19,274 --> 00:05:23,602
When you create an Article, its Banner Image field has an Add media button.

81
00:05:23,602 --> 00:05:24,724
Let's click it.

82
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:30,136
The Select Media dialog holds the same library, with the folder tree, the

83
00:05:30,136 --> 00:05:32,568
Upload files button and the list.

84
00:05:32,568 --> 00:05:36,060
Open Harvest Festival, tick a photo, and click OK.

85
00:05:36,596 --> 00:05:38,318
The field shows the photo.

86
00:05:38,318 --> 00:05:41,762
It keeps the path of the file in the library, so any other

87
00:05:41,762 --> 00:05:44,776
page can use the same file without another upload.

88
00:05:48,976 --> 00:05:52,129
Three optional features extend the library.

89
00:05:52,129 --> 00:05:57,149
Media Slugify gives the folders and files you add clean names, Media TUS

90
00:05:57,149 --> 00:06:02,683
Uploads makes uploads resumable, and Media SignalR keeps open libraries in sync.

91
00:06:02,683 --> 00:06:04,936
A separate video covers them.

92
00:06:06,936 --> 00:06:11,116
The Media Library keeps the files of your site in one place, ready

93
00:06:11,116 --> 00:06:13,206
to upload, organize and reuse.

94
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,716
Thanks for watching.

